The Android integration approach was informed by MirrorMsg by killdano,
licensed AGPL-3.0: https://github.com/killdano/mirrormsg
Message Center's Android and Go integration code is maintained in this repository.

Go's standard library and golang.org/x modules use BSD-style licenses.
Google protobuf uses a BSD-style license; zerolog uses MIT; google/uuid uses BSD.
Their source and notices are included in the dependency-source release archive.
Pictures that phone decoders can't read (such as iPhone Genmoji, which use
HEVC 4:4:4 colour and a monochrome transparency layer) are decoded with
libde265 1.0.16 by struktur AG, licensed LGPL-3.0-or-later, in an isolated
process. Its source and license are in bridge/heic/libde265 and in the
dependency-source release archive. https://github.com/strukturag/libde265
Some interface icon shapes follow Material Design icons by Google, licensed Apache-2.0.
Videos are re-encoded for sending with AndroidX Media3 1.9.3 (Transformer, Effect and their
modules) by The Android Open Source Project, licensed Apache-2.0: https://github.com/androidx/media
Its dependencies (Guava, Kotlin standard library and coroutines, AndroidX annotation, core,
collection, concurrent-futures and exifinterface) are licensed Apache-2.0; JSpecify, Checker
Framework qualifiers and Error Prone annotations use Apache-2.0 or MIT.

Picture text recognition uses Tesseract4Android 4.9.0 by Adaptech s.r.o. (Apache-2.0,
https://github.com/adaptech-cz/Tesseract4Android), which includes Tesseract OCR 5.5.1 (Apache-2.0),
Leptonica 1.85.0 (BSD-2-Clause), libpng 1.6.48 (libpng license) and libjpeg 9f (IJG license).
The English model (eng.traineddata) is from tesseract-ocr/tessdata_fast, Apache-2.0:
https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_fast. Recognition runs on the device.

The emoji picker's names and keywords (app/src/main/assets/emoji.tsv) come from emojibase-data 18.0.0
by Miles Johnson, MIT license (https://github.com/milesj/emojibase), which draws on Unicode CLDR
annotations, Unicode License v3 (https://www.unicode.org/license.txt). Emoji are drawn with the
phone's own emoji font.
